('015860', '7dba7f95-70ef-405e-b3eb-c8a8118318e1', '778', 'Introduction to Comparative Politics', 'Introduction to Comparative Politics, one of the four sub-fields in Political Science, which involves the comparative analysis of political institutions, processes, and outcomes at the national level. Examines how to usefully compare politics in a variety of countries and makes comparisons explicit and systematic in order to determine how governments work, how power is organized and contested at the national level, and how regular people can participate and pursue their interests in different political settings. Includes key concepts, theories, methods, issues, and language. ', 'Not open to students with credit for POLI SCI 182 (or POLI SCI 186 prior to Fall 2017)', 'C', 'POLI SCI 120', 'POLITICAL SCIENCE 120', 4, 4, NULL, NULL, 'S', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'E', 'Fall, Spring', NULL, 'Student Option', 'N', 'N', 120, 2),
