Placement on the wait list does not guarantee enrollment into the class. For our waitlist policy and all FAQs: https://econ.wisc.edu/undergraduate/faq/

Masters students in Economics may enroll into courses designated as Economics Core Electives beginning mid-November for Spring enrollment and mid-April for Fall enrollment. Please email your program manager for more information.

Enrollment for courses designated as Honors in the Economics Department prioritizes enrollment first for Honors-designated students. Enrollment into these classes for any other qualifying student will happen in mid-November for Spring enrollment and mid-April for Fall enrollment. 

Economics does not manage enrollment for cross-listed classes within the Wisconsin School of Business (WSB). The subject notes of the WSB class lists enrollment details. 

Special/non-degree-seeking students should fill out the following form for permission to enroll in Economics undergraduate courses: https://econ.wisc.edu/special-non-degree-seeking-students/. Permission will be granted beginning late November for Spring enrollment and late April for Fall enrollment. Please note that enrollment is not guaranteed.

Undergraduate students with enrollment inquiries should email econadvise@ssc.wisc.edu.'),
